{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt d49fea41cc383dc70d465903e94598a6dc790bd1, these four files contain 13 confirmed prose blocks that can be condensed without behavior change. The former older-SHA ranges mixed prose and code and missed four long owner docstrings/comments. Lines are immutable-base citations, not edit coordinates.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\nA stable ID is the full path plus :: plus the listed suffix. Only these blocks may change.\n\n- src/rebar/_io/_cli.py (3): module-docstring@1-7; export_cli::comment(The factory is the parser of record)@29-37; import_cli::comment(Factory is the parser of record)@102-106.\n- src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py (3): module-docstring@1-8; _coerce_ns-docstring@16-25; create_kwargs-docstring@35-45.\n- src/rebar/_io/_strip.py (1): module-docstring@1-15.\n- src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py (6): module-docstring@1-39; _scan_existing_source_ids-docstring@93-97; import_tickets-docstring@123-134; import_tickets::comment(Chunk size for the batched-commit flush)@184-189; import_tickets::comment(transition_core requires a bounded class)@356-361; import_tickets::comment(Every closeable ticket is still open here)@370-376.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve the argparse-inexpressible token rules and error/output channels; exact nanosecond coercion; source-versus-local-genesis provenance; provider key/comment-id stripping while retaining source_* fields; two-pass/sub-phase ordering; source_id idempotence; chunk boundaries; deferred push; children-before-parents; and the ordinary-close/no-force invariant. Real consumers are export/import CLI handlers and the locked write/reducer paths; no allowlisted docstring is read via __d